package engine

var delegationDescriptions = map[string]string{
	"spawn_agent": "Delegate a bounded task when authorized. Send independent spawns together. Set overlap=true on a foreground child when you can do independent work in parallel. Continue that work after admission, wait for the child only when you need its result, and integrate the results before finishing. Overlapping children stay owned by this turn and completed results arrive automatically. Ordinary foreground calls wait before the parent's next step; detached background work completes separately. Extra children queue at the concurrency limit. Keep the returned session and turn IDs.\n\n" +
		"Give the child the goal, scope and expected result. Include established findings and path:line references so its separate conversation can start with the remaining work. For a new child, follow the team instructions and pass the exact key of the role whose responsibilities fit. Omit role to use this turn's model when roleless delegation is allowed. Children inherit the worktree, mode and permissions. A named read-only role runs in Plan. Children cannot delegate. A registered worktree or disjoint file scope keeps parallel edits separate.\n\n" +
		"Use guide_agent for follow-ups to an existing child. To explicitly continue verified unfinished work with spawn_agent in an idle child, pass its exact returned session ID and omit role to keep its role, model, worktree, settings and history. Check list_subagents when recovering earlier work; do not restart active work or treat a title as evidence of the task. Do not restart a cancelled or separately stopped child without an explicit request to resume that child.",
	"guide_agent":    "Give new directions to a child owned by this conversation. Copy its exact returned session ID; never reconstruct it. Running guidance is durable: the child receives it after its entire current tool batch settles and before its next model request; an in-flight model response yields at that boundary. This returns a queued guidance receipt, not the child's final result. Explicit follow-up to an idle child starts a new foreground task in the same session, preserving its history, role, model, worktree and permissions. The task uses current package settings. Busy queued or stopping children cannot be restarted. For recovery, verify the same unfinished task from prior evidence, not its title. Do not restart a cancelled or separately stopped child without an explicit request to resume that child.",
	"wait_agent":     "Collect a child's durable final answer and status within a bounded observation window. Launch ready children and finish independent work first. Wait only for a result needed now or for an explicit request to wait. Send independent waits together. A pending receipt refers to the same execution; do not repeat the spawn or poll it. Use the exact returned session and, when known, turn ID. New guidance returns early with guidance_pending so the parent can apply it.",
	"list_subagents": "Inspect this conversation's direct subagent sessions across turns, not the role catalog. Returns only session and turn IDs, assigned title and role, status, queued pause, and stop_reason when explicit stop evidence is available for that turn. A missing reason does not rule out a stop. Pass next_before back as before until null. Listing never resumes work. Only continue a child when the user continues the same unfinished task and prior evidence matches its scope, not just its title. Reuse completed results unchanged; do not reopen running, queued or stopping work. Never resume a cancelled or separately stopped child without an explicit request to resume that child.",
}
